# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Packages in Omarchy's own list (install/omarchy-base.packages) that the
# phone image leaves out on purpose. Packages that aren't built for aarch64
# are left out anyway and listed in the image's MANIFEST. One that is built
# but whose dependencies pacman cannot meet stops the build with pacman's
# reasons; list it here only if it can never work on a phone.
# Registers binfmt handlers to run other architectures' binaries: a laptop's job
qemu-user-static-binfmt
# Hyprbars titlebars for floating workspaces (Omarchy 4.5): a plugin pinned to
# one exact Hyprland version, so it skews against our packages/hyprland build
# and would pull Omarchy's Hyprland over ours (#433); a phone has no floating
# workspaces to put titlebars on
omarchy-hyprland-titlebars
# Superwhisper (Omarchy 4.5's list): proprietary. Images carry no proprietary
# preinstalls; the phone's dictation is Voxtype (omamobile-voice). An owner
# who wants it can install it.
superwhisper-bin
# OWE, Omarchy 4.5's video wallpaper engine, which also feeds the lock screen
# its frames. Updated phones don't get it: the migration that starts it
# (1789764927) is held as an unreviewed video pipeline on a phone, so a new
# image leaves it out too, and the two agree. Take it off this list when the
# hold is released.
owe
# Input-method engines for Fcitx (Omarchy 4.5's list). The on-screen keyboard
# holds the phone's input-method slot and the Fcitx migration is held on
# updated phones, so nothing could use them; Fcitx itself stays, as in 4.0.
fcitx5-chewing
fcitx5-chinese-addons
fcitx5-hangul
fcitx5-mozc
fcitx5-table-extra
